# Build context hygiene for apps/*/Dockerfile (repo-root context — every app's Dockerfile needs the
# root manifests, all of packages/*, and its own source; see each Dockerfile's header comment).
# Keep this in sync with .gitignore's intent, but note it can't be app-specific: the same context
# is sent regardless of which app's -f apps/<app>/Dockerfile is built, so nothing app-scoped
# (e.g. "the other 7 apps/*/src") can be excluded here.

# Dependencies — reinstalled fresh inside the build (bun install --frozen-lockfile)
**/node_modules

# Build output — images build from source; nothing here is ever a build input
**/dist
**/.tanstack
**/.vite
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/CHANGELOG.md

# VCS, CI, and editor/IDE tooling — never needed inside the image
.git
.github
**/.github
.husky
.serena
.claude
**/.claude
**/.vscode
**/.idea

# Tests and their artifacts — not part of any app's production build
**/tests
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
**/.playwright-mcp
**/stats.html
**/count.txt

# Secrets — env values are supplied at container runtime, never baked into a layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Docs — large and irrelevant to the build. `shadow build` copies README.md/LICENSE into a
# package's dist/ *if present* (skipped silently otherwise), so excluding them costs nothing.
**/*.md
**/docs

# OS / logs
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/logs
